{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AMgjTaTrREfrHbt7vaDMqx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tphase: 01-retry-budget\n3\treviewed: 2026-11-02T00:00:00Z\n4\tdepth: standard\n5\tfiles_reviewed: 2\n6\tfiles_reviewed_list:\n7\t  - probe/__init__.py\n8\t  - probe/budget.py\n9\tfindings:\n10\t  critical: 0\n11\t  warning: 2\n12\t  info: 2\n13\t  total: 4\n14\tstatus: issues_found\n15\t---\n16\t\n17\t# Phase 1: Code Review Report\n18\t\n19\t**Reviewed:** 2026-11-02\n20\t**Depth:** standard\n21\t**Files Reviewed:** 2\n22\t**Status:** issues_found\n23\t\n24\t## Summary\n25\t\n26\tReviewed `probe/__init__.py` (empty, as the plan requires; not a finding) and `probe/budget.py` (10 lines, diff `8cc4245..HEAD`). The code does what the plan says: `DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS: int = 120` and `deadline_after` returns `start_secs + budget`. I ran `python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -v` in this worktree: 2 tests, OK. `probe/__pycache__` is git-ignored and not tracked. There is no CLAUDE.md or project skills directory.\n27\t\n28\tThe code has no logic defect. The concerns are about the decision behind the constant and about nothing protecting it:\n29\t\n30\t- The plan's blocking human decision gate was resolved by the orchestrator, not a human (WR-01).\n31\t- No test or code pins the value, so the plan's reasoning can regress without any failure (WR-02).\n32\t\n33\tWhat this review does not establish: the 90 s failover and 240 s pager figures come from the plan, and I could not check them. There are no callers of `deadline_after` in the reviewed scope, so behavior in a real retry loop is untested.\n34\t\n35\t## Warnings\n36\t\n37\t### WR-01: Plan's blocking human decision gate was resolved without a human\n38\t\n39\t**File:** `probe/budget.py:5`\n40\t**Issue:** Task 1 in `01-01-PLAN.md` is `checkpoint:decision gate=\"blocking-human\"` and the plan has `autonomous: false`. The SUMMARY (key-decisions, Decisions Made, Deviations) says no